{"name":"Red Pegasus","hex":"#dd0000","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"pegasus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Pegasus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pegasus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Akai Pegasus","blocks":[{"text":"Akai Pegasus , is a Japanese manga series written and illustrated by Motoka Murakami. It was serialized in Shogakukan's Weekly Shōnen Sunday from June 1975 to September 1977."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5e/Akai_Pegasus_vol_1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akai_Pegasus"},{"title":"Pegasus","blocks":[{"text":"Pegasus is a winged horse in Greek mythology, usually depicted as a white stallion. He was sired by Poseidon, in his role as horse-god, and foaled by Medusa, one of three Gorgon sisters. Pegasus was the brother of Chrysaor, both born from Medusa's blood when their mother was decapitated by Perseus. Greco-Roman poets wrote about his ascent to heaven after his birth and his obeisance to Zeus, who instructed him to bring lightning and thunder from Olympus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Lakonian_Black-Figure_Kylix%3B_detached_fragments.jpg/330px-Lakonian_Black-Figure_Kylix%3B_detached_fragments.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pegasus"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Pelike_Bellerophon_Louvre_G535.jpg/500px-Pelike_Bellerophon_Louvre_G535.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Pelike_Bellerophon_Louvre_G535.jpg/1280px-Pelike_Bellerophon_Louvre_G535.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Pelike_Bellerophon_Louvre_G535.jpg/500px-Pelike_Bellerophon_Louvre_G535.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bellerophon mounted on Pegasus fighting the Chimera, side A from an Attic red-figure pelike","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APelike_Bellerophon_Louvre_G535.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Bellerophon_riding_Pegasus_and_killing_the_Chimera%2C_Roman_mosaic%2C_the_Rolin_Museum_in_Autun%2C_France%2C_2nd_to_3rd_century_AD.jpg/500px-Bellerophon_riding_Pegasus_and_killing_the_Chimera%2C_Roman_mosaic%2C_the_Rolin_Museum_in_Autun%2C_France%2C_2nd_to_3rd_century_AD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&